title: 'M1.8 slice 2: per-task endpoint choice is kernel-side, steer joins the in-flight turn''s permit'
summary: session.open has no endpoint param in §5, so per-task choice = first endpoint in signed order capable for the task floor; session.send{steer} with a turn in flight writes turn.steer under that turn's permit (no new permit, no turn.sent); idle steer is a plain send; Claude sessions refuse steer
